\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 2. Resolution A \'97 Community Cardinality\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Decision status: APPROVED AND RESOLVED
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 2.1 Authoritative cardinality\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 The approved relationship is:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Community 1 
\f2 \uc0\u8594 
\f0  many CivicContent records
\f1\b0 \

\f0\b Each CivicContent record belongs to exactly one Community.
\f1\b0 \
Community represents the First Step catalog and delivery partition in which content is managed and presented.\
Community does 
\f0\b not
\f1\b0  represent the complete geographic reach, service area, jurisdiction, or resident eligibility of the underlying program, law, organization, or event.\
Consequently, Community ownership must not be used to infer whether a resident is eligible for a particular program or service.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 2.2 Multi-community capability\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 First Step v2 must be architecturally capable of maintaining Community A's catalog and Community B's catalog simultaneously.\
Resident-facing operations must establish the relevant Community before querying or selecting content from its catalog.\
This is a requirement for community-scoped catalog operations, not for multiple Community memberships on the same CivicContent record.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 2.3 Required v2 implementation behavior\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Preserve singular 
\f3\fs26 communityId
\f1\fs24  / Community ownership.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Maintain Community as a first-class domain concept.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Validate Community references and catalog partition integrity.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Require Community-scoped resident retrieval.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Prevent implicit Wilmington-only assumptions in shared services and selection logic.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Keep Community ownership distinct from physical location, service area, and provider-published eligibility information.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

