\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 3. Resolution B \'97 Featured-Topic P5 Alignment\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Decision status: APPROVED AND RESOLVED
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 3.1 Governing principle\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Help first, context second.
\f1\b0 \
Featured Topics must reflect the strength of relevant, resident-actionable information and opportunities, rather than simply the total number of classified content records.\
Relevant law and policy information may help distinguish Topics when appropriate, but contextual information must not displace stronger resident-actionable inventory solely because it is more numerous or more recent.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 3.2 Authoritative selection hierarchy\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 IM-06 must preserve the complete approved P5 ordering:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Resident-actionable inventory:
\f1\b0  Strength/count of current qualifying programs, services, resources, and access opportunities.\
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Featured-role completeness:
\f1\b0  Availability of qualifying TIMELY, DURABLE, and VISUAL content.\
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Direct resident-action opportunities:
\f1\b0  Strength of meaningful opportunities for residents to take a next step.\
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Relevant law or policy context:
\f1\b0  Explicitly classified and meaningfully related legal or policy information, used as a later discriminator.\
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	5	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Catalog/approval newness:
\f1\b0  Newer qualifying content only after stronger criteria are equal.\
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	6	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Stable Topic key:
\f1\b0  Immutable deterministic fallback independent of collection iteration order.\
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	7	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Admin diagnostic:
\f1\b0  Report cases where selection reaches a technical rather than meaningful fallback, without interrupting resident delivery.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 This hierarchy is deterministic and based on approved, explicit metadata.\
It does not create an AI ranking system, engagement score, personalized recommendation model, or permanent featured property.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

